1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,342
Every forbidden zone on Earth

2
00:00:01,372 --> 00:00:03,316
looks like a warning built to save you.

3
00:00:04,052 --> 00:00:06,215
Step inside three locked-off places,

4
00:00:06,322 --> 00:00:08,242
and the real danger flips completely.

5
00:00:08,522 --> 00:00:10,230
Around Chernobyl's shattered reactor,

6
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:11,987
a giant exclusion zone still

7
00:00:12,017 --> 00:00:13,698
bars normal human life.

8
00:00:14,442 --> 00:00:17,287
Radiation there burned whole pine stands rust-red,

9
00:00:17,383 --> 00:00:19,689
creating what workers named the Red Forest.

10
00:00:19,905 --> 00:00:21,161
Yet once people vanished,

11
00:00:21,259 --> 00:00:22,708
wildlife surged back.

12
00:00:23,462 --> 00:00:25,820
Gray wolves, wild horses, and deer

13
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:27,404
multiplied across empty towns

14
00:00:27,434 --> 00:00:29,403
faster than in nearby reserves.

15
00:00:29,653 --> 00:00:31,803
Even stranger, robots probing inside

16
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,886
the reactor walls found pitch-black fungi

17
00:00:33,916 --> 00:00:35,524
growing toward radiation.

18
00:00:36,268 --> 00:00:37,888
Packed with dark melanin pigment,

19
00:00:37,972 --> 00:00:40,694
those fungi harvest lethal gamma rays for energy.

20
00:00:40,963 --> 00:00:43,223
In southwestern France, Lascaux Cave

21
00:00:43,253 --> 00:00:45,259
is locked for the exact opposite reason.

22
00:00:46,012 --> 00:00:47,932
Humans aren't banned to save visitors—

23
00:00:48,042 --> 00:00:49,083
we are the poison.

24
00:00:49,305 --> 00:00:50,910
For 17,000 years,

25
00:00:50,971 --> 00:00:53,404
prehistoric animal paintings survived inside

26
00:00:53,434 --> 00:00:55,204
cool, sealed limestone air.

27
00:00:55,958 --> 00:00:58,162
When crowds poured in, human breath,

28
00:00:58,297 --> 00:00:59,814
body heat, and shoe spores

29
00:00:59,844 --> 00:01:01,677
triggered white mold that ate the art.

30
00:01:02,431 --> 00:01:04,294
France sealed the real cave forever

31
00:01:04,324 --> 00:01:06,219
and built an exact copy nearby.

32
00:01:06,458 --> 00:01:08,614
Off Iceland's coast, Surtsey Island

33
00:01:08,644 --> 00:01:10,950
bans humans for an even stricter purpose:

34
00:01:11,034 --> 00:01:12,090
pure creation.

35
00:01:12,835 --> 00:01:14,692
When an undersea volcano boiled up

36
00:01:14,722 --> 00:01:15,398
in 1963,

37
00:01:16,254 --> 00:01:18,890
scientists quarantined the barren rock immediately.

38
00:01:19,636 --> 00:01:22,052
Researchers scrub every seed from their boots—

39
00:01:22,173 --> 00:01:24,638
and when one stray tomato sprouted in ash,

40
00:01:24,746 --> 00:01:25,802
they ripped it out.

41
00:01:26,043 --> 00:01:27,612
Carried only by ocean waves

42
00:01:27,642 --> 00:01:28,651
and nesting gulls,

43
00:01:28,753 --> 00:01:31,353
60 plant species turned black lava green.

44
00:01:32,125 --> 00:01:34,257
That doesn't mean radiation is harmless,

45
00:01:34,334 --> 00:01:35,946
or that sealed caves ever recover

46
00:01:35,976 --> 00:01:38,260
once human crowds break their balance.

47
00:01:38,495 --> 00:01:40,008
Some forbidden zones lock us out

48
00:01:40,038 --> 00:01:41,552
to keep our bodies alive.

49
00:01:42,324 --> 00:01:43,860
The rarest ones lock us out

50
00:01:43,890 --> 00:01:46,477
because a single human footprint changes everything.
